infographic sequence-timeline-simple
data
  title The Nest lifecycle: init fires bottom-up, shutdown reverses it
  desc The shutdown half (last three hooks) fires only if main.ts called enableShutdownHooks()
  sequences
    - label Build DI graph
      desc Every provider constructed — no lifecycle hook fires yet
    - label onModuleInit
      desc Per module, children before parents (bottom-up)
    - label onApplicationBootstrap
      desc Once, after every module — the whole graph is live
    - label SIGTERM
      desc Caught only if enableShutdownHooks() was called
    - label onModuleDestroy
      desc Reverse: dependents before deps; await pool.end()
    - label beforeApplicationShutdown
      desc Pre-close hook; receives the signal string
    - label onApplicationShutdown
      desc Final teardown; receives signal, then process exits
theme
  palette #6366f1 #8b5cf6 #f43f5e
